From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ishan Chattopadhyaya <ishan@apache.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 19:36:48 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] reader: seek explicit term sets block by block

ExplicitTermsEnum now does one forward exact seek per requested term.
TermsEnum::blockFor finds the term's block through a TrieReader::Cursor
that resumes each trie descent where the previous target diverged, the
next candidate's block is prefetched while the current one is handled,
and seekExactInBlock scans the block reading only prefix lengths and
suffix bytes. A lookup that takes one term from a block reads only that
term's postings metadata entries (svbValueAt) instead of decoding every
term's.
